1
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:18,200
Stay back!

2
00:00:28,560 --> 00:00:29,880
He should've said, "Heel."

3
00:00:52,160 --> 00:00:53,160
Slag it!

4
00:00:56,560 --> 00:00:58,520
He's really got a delicate touch,
Dee Dee.

5
00:00:58,600 --> 00:01:00,280
Delicate like a moose, Dee Dee.

6
00:01:03,480 --> 00:01:06,800
I hate ripping this heavy junk.
Give me cash cards any day.

7
00:01:08,520 --> 00:01:11,920
Zip it, Bonk.
Plan is, get in and get out fast.

8
00:01:14,960 --> 00:01:18,240
It's a school night, boys and girls.
I'm gonna have to call your folks.

9
00:01:43,040 --> 00:01:44,320
Bonk! Don't!

10
00:01:45,280 --> 00:01:46,640
Yeah, Bonk. Don't.

11
00:02:33,600 --> 00:02:35,800
Let's go! Dee Dee, open the door.

12
00:02:35,880 --> 00:02:36,880
- On the double!
- On the double!

13
00:03:05,800 --> 00:03:06,800
Incoming!

14
00:03:16,560 --> 00:03:18,320
Bonk! You moron! Get back here!

15
00:04:00,640 --> 00:04:02,280
You got a death wish, Bats!

16
00:04:02,480 --> 00:04:05,040
And here I thought
I was just being a good citizen.

17
00:04:09,880 --> 00:04:10,880
Got you, sis!

18
00:04:15,440 --> 00:04:16,760
Flagpole.

19
00:04:17,240 --> 00:04:18,240
What did you say?

20
00:04:18,440 --> 00:04:19,760
Flagpole.

21
00:04:34,320 --> 00:04:35,320
Come on.

22
00:05:02,760 --> 00:05:04,520
That ain't coming
out of my allowance.

23
00:07:16,480 --> 00:07:17,680
Still got it.

24
00:07:29,480 --> 00:07:31,080
How did it go with the Jokerz?

25
00:07:31,960 --> 00:07:33,880
I broke up the robbery,
but it was weird.

26
00:07:35,440 --> 00:07:37,000
Third time this month
that particular gang

27
00:07:37,080 --> 00:07:38,840
was trying to intercept
high-tech machinery.

28
00:07:38,920 --> 00:07:40,200
Jokerz don't use that stuff.

29
00:07:40,680 --> 00:07:44,000
They're probably fencing it.
Corporate espionage is big business.

30
00:07:44,520 --> 00:07:46,800
I may as well sit tight
until I can get another shot at 'em.

31
00:07:48,680 --> 00:07:49,880
Hey, looky here.

32
00:07:50,160 --> 00:07:51,200
That's right, Tom.

33
00:07:51,280 --> 00:07:54,360
Today, Gotham billionaire Bruce Wayne
stunned the financial world

34
00:07:54,440 --> 00:07:57,840
with his plan to resume active
leadership of Wayne Enterprises.

35
00:07:57,920 --> 00:08:00,920
While shareholders have generally
welcomed Wayne's return

36
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:02,880
support from some key members
of the Wayne board

37
00:08:02,960 --> 00:08:04,680
has been oddly lukewarm.

38
00:08:04,760 --> 00:08:08,120
Company operations manager,
Jordan Pryce, offered this comment.

39
00:08:08,200 --> 00:08:11,080
I, of course, join the rest
of our Wayne Enterprises family

40
00:08:11,160 --> 00:08:15,280
in welcoming back our most valuable
senior resource, Bruce Wayne.

41
00:08:15,360 --> 00:08:18,720
I'm sure we'll all profit
from his years of experience.

42
00:08:18,800 --> 00:08:21,000
Still, the day-to-day rigors
of running a vast

43
00:08:21,080 --> 00:08:23,360
multinational conglomerate
would be stressful

44
00:08:23,440 --> 00:08:24,680
even for a young man.

45
00:08:24,760 --> 00:08:26,920
I hope Mr. Wayne
is up to the challenge.

46
00:08:27,040 --> 00:08:28,800
He's not bitter... much.

47
00:08:29,200 --> 00:08:31,400
Pryce was next in line
for the top spot.

48
00:08:31,760 --> 00:08:34,600
My return torpedoed any dreams
he had of succession.

49
00:08:35,400 --> 00:08:38,200
- You gonna keep him around?
- If he'll stay on my terms.

50
00:08:38,600 --> 00:08:42,200
I've worked long and hard to regain
control of my family's company.

51
00:08:42,280 --> 00:08:43,840
And I won't hand it over again.

52
00:08:43,920 --> 00:08:45,920
Pryce can either
get with that program

53
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:47,720
or start e-mailing his résumé.

54
00:08:47,880 --> 00:08:48,880
With all the long hours

55
00:08:48,960 --> 00:08:50,440
you're planning
on putting in at the office

56
00:08:50,520 --> 00:08:52,280
does this mean
you'll have less time for...

57
00:08:53,200 --> 00:08:54,560
Who sleeps anymore?

58
00:08:58,160 --> 00:08:59,160
You okay?

59
00:08:59,240 --> 00:09:01,400
You know the Jokerz
are going in for splicing now?

60
00:09:01,480 --> 00:09:03,360
Crazy hyena-boy
nearly took a bite out of me.

61
00:09:03,680 --> 00:09:05,600
No way I could have
explained that to Dana.

62
00:09:05,680 --> 00:09:07,160
You're not going out now?

63
00:09:07,240 --> 00:09:08,840
The night is young, and so am I.

64
00:09:08,920 --> 00:09:11,680
I think a good night's rest
might be more beneficial.

65
00:09:11,760 --> 00:09:13,680
Like you said, who sleeps anymore?

66
00:09:22,120 --> 00:09:23,400
Up and at 'em, Terry.

67
00:09:26,120 --> 00:09:28,640
You can doze
on Bruce Wayne's time, not mine.

68
00:09:29,320 --> 00:09:30,320
Sorry, Dane.

69
00:09:56,040 --> 00:09:57,280
Great song, huh?

70
00:09:58,640 --> 00:10:00,760
Did you see the squid Blade's with?

71
00:10:00,840 --> 00:10:01,840
P.U.!

72
00:10:04,080 --> 00:10:05,720
Ter, my head's on fire.

73
00:10:06,440 --> 00:10:07,480
You look good.

74
00:10:08,400 --> 00:10:09,600
McGinnis!

75
00:10:14,520 --> 00:10:17,240
Sorry, babe. Guess the day
was longer than I thought.

76
00:10:20,360 --> 00:10:21,680
Let's sit this one out.

77
00:10:23,440 --> 00:10:25,360
Coffee. And leave the pot.

78
00:10:30,160 --> 00:10:32,080
Batman showed up
and we had to ditch.

79
00:10:32,280 --> 00:10:35,520
We were able to save this.
The console's memory board.

80
00:10:37,320 --> 00:10:38,760
I know it's not much, but...

81
00:10:39,240 --> 00:10:41,920
It's not much? It's nothing.

82
00:10:44,960 --> 00:10:46,080
Losers.

83
00:10:47,040 --> 00:10:48,040
All of you.

84
00:10:48,240 --> 00:10:52,240
A disgrace to the name Joker.
Why, in my day...

85
00:10:52,320 --> 00:10:53,720
In your day?

86
00:10:53,800 --> 00:10:55,880
Ever since you conned
your way into this gang

87
00:10:55,960 --> 00:10:59,080
it's been "your day" this
and "your day" that.

88
00:10:59,160 --> 00:11:00,200
Bonk.

89
00:11:00,280 --> 00:11:01,840
Your day is over, old man.

90
00:11:01,920 --> 00:11:03,840
Even if you are who you say you are.

91
00:11:03,920 --> 00:11:06,000
And personally,
I think you're a fake.

92
00:11:06,800 --> 00:11:09,040
Brave new world...

93
00:11:09,120 --> 00:11:11,200
that has such yutzes in it.

94
00:11:11,560 --> 00:11:14,160
He's got us running around
ripping a lot of geek junk

95
00:11:14,240 --> 00:11:15,280
but no cash!

96
00:11:15,720 --> 00:11:18,560
He won't tell us what his plan is,
if he even has one.

97
00:11:18,880 --> 00:11:20,520
I want out!

98
00:11:21,040 --> 00:11:22,520
If you insist.

99
00:11:25,960 --> 00:11:28,960
Hey, man. Take it easy.
I... I was just kidding.

100
00:11:32,760 --> 00:11:34,120
So was I.

101
00:11:43,720 --> 00:11:45,960
Oops. No, I wasn't.

102
00:11:48,280 --> 00:11:50,760
That's also how we did it in my day.

103
00:11:54,680 --> 00:11:56,400
You know, kids, a lot has changed

104
00:11:56,480 --> 00:11:58,640
while your old Uncle Joker's
been away.

105
00:11:58,720 --> 00:12:00,840
New Gotham, new rules.

106
00:12:01,160 --> 00:12:02,960
Even a new Batman.

107
00:12:05,120 --> 00:12:07,600
But now, I'm tanned, I'm rested

108
00:12:07,680 --> 00:12:11,480
and I'm ready to give this old town
a wedgie again!

109
00:12:12,960 --> 00:12:13,960
Great, boss.

110
00:12:15,160 --> 00:12:18,800
Ghoul, my boy, we're going
to need another systems scanner.

111
00:12:18,880 --> 00:12:21,040
Who's got one
they'd be willing to donate?

112
00:12:21,320 --> 00:12:22,320
Checking.

113
00:12:23,040 --> 00:12:25,400
What we're after is cutting-edge.

114
00:12:25,480 --> 00:12:27,560
These are the only other places
we'd find one.

115
00:12:28,520 --> 00:12:29,600
Nope.

116
00:12:30,120 --> 00:12:31,120
No.

117
00:12:32,400 --> 00:12:35,160
What, there?
Security's gonna be tight!

118
00:12:35,760 --> 00:12:38,600
Oh, yes. But think of the fun.

119
00:12:44,480 --> 00:12:45,640
Good evening, Mr. Wayne.

120
00:12:46,120 --> 00:12:49,040
Ms. Carr. You remember my assistant,
Terry McGinnis?

121
00:12:49,120 --> 00:12:51,240
Of course.
I'm glad you could join us, Terry.

122
00:12:52,360 --> 00:12:53,360
Everyone is here.

123
00:12:54,040 --> 00:12:56,600
Well, everyone except Mr. Pryce,
unfortunately.

124
00:12:56,680 --> 00:12:58,000
That's no surprise.

125
00:12:59,240 --> 00:13:00,840
May I have your attention, please?

126
00:13:01,240 --> 00:13:04,560
It's my pleasure to welcome back
the guiding light of this company...

127
00:13:06,200 --> 00:13:07,400
Bruce Wayne.

128
00:13:14,520 --> 00:13:15,560
Thank you, Joyce.

129
00:13:16,240 --> 00:13:18,000
It's a pleasure to see you all again.

130
00:13:18,080 --> 00:13:19,800
In the future, I hope to...

131
00:13:27,360 --> 00:13:30,480
spend time getting to know
each member of our company

132
00:13:30,560 --> 00:13:32,360
learning about you individually.

133
00:13:53,360 --> 00:13:55,640
Security! Emergency on terrace level.

134
00:14:00,840 --> 00:14:02,120
Hey! Look out!

135
00:14:17,240 --> 00:14:19,080
- You gonna be okay?
- Go to work.

136
00:14:22,080 --> 00:14:24,080
Well, if it isn't old Mr. Wayne.

137
00:14:24,840 --> 00:14:26,040
So debonair.

138
00:14:26,880 --> 00:14:27,880
So dapper.

139
00:14:29,920 --> 00:14:30,920
So decrepit.

140
00:14:44,280 --> 00:14:45,680
Hello, Gotham!

141
00:14:45,760 --> 00:14:47,600
Joker's back in town!

142
00:14:50,480 --> 00:14:51,680
It can't be.

143
00:14:52,080 --> 00:14:56,200
Oh, no, your old eyes
do not deceive you, Brucie!

144
00:14:56,280 --> 00:14:58,960
After all,
who'd know me better than you?

145
00:15:01,640 --> 00:15:02,760
Back off, gruesome.

146
00:15:07,360 --> 00:15:08,840
The new boy.

147
00:15:08,920 --> 00:15:11,160
Ears are too long,
and I miss the cape

148
00:15:11,240 --> 00:15:14,000
but not too shabby.
Not too shabby at all.

149
00:15:14,080 --> 00:15:15,080
Woof!

150
00:15:26,520 --> 00:15:28,200
How's it coming, boys?

151
00:15:28,280 --> 00:15:29,600
We're home free.

152
00:15:29,680 --> 00:15:31,160
Then I'll see you there.

153
00:15:35,560 --> 00:15:37,200
Time to go, Dee Dee.

154
00:16:13,120 --> 00:16:15,280
Well? What's it gonna be, Batfake?

155
00:16:44,200 --> 00:16:46,400
I know what you're thinking.
I messed up.

156
00:16:47,120 --> 00:16:49,320
I let the clown go
in order to save those people.

157
00:16:49,560 --> 00:16:50,760
You did the right thing.

158
00:16:51,480 --> 00:16:53,200
So, the Joker, huh?

159
00:16:54,160 --> 00:16:56,080
Looks pretty spry
for a guy who's gotta be, what?

160
00:16:56,160 --> 00:16:57,160
Mid-eighties?

161
00:16:59,160 --> 00:17:00,280
Any theories on that?

162
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:03,440
Clone? Robot?

163
00:17:03,800 --> 00:17:06,800
Suspended animation due to floating
around frozen in a block of ice?

164
00:17:07,360 --> 00:17:08,600
Shut up and drive.

165
00:17:10,440 --> 00:17:11,440
Yes, sir.

166
00:17:18,320 --> 00:17:20,480
This was the scene
just three hours ago

167
00:17:20,560 --> 00:17:22,800
as a man claiming to be
the legendary Joker

168
00:17:22,880 --> 00:17:23,880
disrupted a ceremony

169
00:17:23,960 --> 00:17:26,480
at the newly-opened
Wayne Enterprises building.

170
00:17:26,560 --> 00:17:28,280
Honey, what're you watching?

171
00:17:28,360 --> 00:17:29,960
Adding to the drama
was the appearance

172
00:17:30,080 --> 00:17:32,320
of another legendary Gotham icon,
the Batman

173
00:17:32,400 --> 00:17:35,560
who engaged his one-time foe
in a stunning aerial battle.

174
00:17:35,640 --> 00:17:36,720
Honey?

175
00:17:37,040 --> 00:17:38,440
It's nothing, sweetheart.

176
00:17:40,840 --> 00:17:41,840
Nothing.

177
00:17:51,160 --> 00:17:52,160
Go away.

178
00:17:52,560 --> 00:17:53,600
Morning, Commish.

179
00:17:53,680 --> 00:17:56,160
You understand English,
McGinnis? Scram.

180
00:17:56,240 --> 00:17:59,520
Love to. But first,
what can you tell me about clowns?

181
00:17:59,760 --> 00:18:01,520
In this town, they're never funny.

182
00:18:02,080 --> 00:18:03,080
I noticed that.

183
00:18:06,360 --> 00:18:08,200
- Now, this Joker...
- Drop it, kid.

184
00:18:08,680 --> 00:18:10,240
That's what
the old man's been saying.

185
00:18:10,320 --> 00:18:11,320
Listen to him.

186
00:18:11,720 --> 00:18:14,160
Hey, look, I know this fruitcake
was one of the big, bad guys

187
00:18:14,240 --> 00:18:15,760
from the cape-and-cowl days.

188
00:18:15,840 --> 00:18:17,000
He was more than that.

189
00:18:17,280 --> 00:18:19,760
What? A garden-variety wacko
who threatened people

190
00:18:19,840 --> 00:18:22,040
with whoopee cushions
and squirting flowers?

191
00:18:22,120 --> 00:18:24,040
- Big deal. I'm shaking.
- McGinnis!

192
00:18:28,400 --> 00:18:31,640
The Joker, the real Joker,
was unlike anyone you've ever faced.

193
00:18:31,720 --> 00:18:33,640
And for your sake,
I hope you never do.

194
00:18:33,720 --> 00:18:35,960
If Bruce wants you to drop it,
then drop it.

195
00:18:37,640 --> 00:18:39,160
Commissioner,
your nine o'clock is here.

196
00:18:39,240 --> 00:18:40,240
Send him in.

197
00:18:40,960 --> 00:18:41,960
You were leaving?

198
00:18:42,400 --> 00:18:43,520
Figure I was.

199
00:18:55,160 --> 00:18:58,120
- Thanks for seeing me, Barb.
- That's what I'm here for.

200
00:19:18,080 --> 00:19:20,920
A countdown of victims
that will end at midnight

201
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:23,960
unless our dear Dark Knight
stops me first!

202
00:19:28,040 --> 00:19:31,280
Hello, Gotham. Joker's back in town!

203
00:19:39,320 --> 00:19:40,320
It's funny.

204
00:19:40,840 --> 00:19:43,520
I know about all of your other major
enemies but you never mention him.

205
00:19:44,560 --> 00:19:47,800
- He was the biggest, wasn't he?
- It wasn't a popularity contest.

206
00:19:48,760 --> 00:19:51,200
He was a psychopath. A monster.

207
00:19:51,840 --> 00:19:54,680
So how is it possible he could still
be around after all this time?

208
00:19:55,120 --> 00:19:56,160
It's not possible.

209
00:19:56,720 --> 00:19:58,160
He died years ago.

210
00:19:58,880 --> 00:19:59,880
You're sure?

211
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:01,200
I was there.

212
00:20:05,480 --> 00:20:07,080
You killed him, didn't you?

213
00:20:09,120 --> 00:20:10,440
He was gonna do something so terrible

214
00:20:10,520 --> 00:20:11,680
you had no other choice.

215
00:20:12,200 --> 00:20:14,320
- Terry...
- That was it, wasn't it?

216
00:20:18,400 --> 00:20:20,520
I want you to give back
the Batman suit.

217
00:20:21,160 --> 00:20:23,320
What? Why?

218
00:20:23,400 --> 00:20:25,320
There is no reason for you
to continue.

219
00:20:26,120 --> 00:20:28,720
You've made your father's killers
pay for his murder.

220
00:20:28,800 --> 00:20:32,800
Then put your own needs aside to help
the city when it most needed a hero.

221
00:20:33,480 --> 00:20:36,280
You've honored the reputation
of Batman many times over

222
00:20:36,360 --> 00:20:37,560
and for that, I thank you.

223
00:20:37,880 --> 00:20:39,000
Then why?

224
00:20:39,400 --> 00:20:42,480
I had no right to force this life
on you or anyone else.

225
00:20:43,240 --> 00:20:46,240
Hey. I was the one who broke in
and swiped the suit, remember?

226
00:20:46,760 --> 00:20:48,040
Yes, there was my dad's murder

227
00:20:48,120 --> 00:20:50,440
but we come
from two different worlds, Mr. Wayne.

228
00:20:50,920 --> 00:20:53,080
I wasn't like you
or the kids you took in.

229
00:20:54,520 --> 00:20:56,280
I was a pretty bad kid once.

230
00:20:56,840 --> 00:20:58,880
Ran with a rough crowd,
broke a lot of laws

231
00:20:58,960 --> 00:21:00,520
to say nothing of my folks' hearts.

232
00:21:01,040 --> 00:21:02,440
The kind of punk
you wouldn't have wasted

233
00:21:02,520 --> 00:21:04,080
a second punch on back in that day.

234
00:21:04,560 --> 00:21:05,560
Your point?

235
00:21:06,080 --> 00:21:08,520
I'm trying to make up for past sins.

236
00:21:09,160 --> 00:21:11,160
The state says my three months
in juvie wiped me clean

237
00:21:11,240 --> 00:21:12,640
but my soul tells me different.

238
00:21:13,200 --> 00:21:14,600
Every time I put on that suit

239
00:21:14,680 --> 00:21:16,920
it's my chance to help people
who are in trouble.

240
00:21:17,920 --> 00:21:19,520
I guess on a personal level

241
00:21:20,160 --> 00:21:22,640
it's a chance to look like
a worthwhile human being again.

242
00:21:23,440 --> 00:21:25,120
In my eyes, if no one else's.

243
00:21:27,200 --> 00:21:28,720
It's what I want, Bruce.

244
00:21:31,040 --> 00:21:32,240
Stupid kid.

245
00:21:32,600 --> 00:21:35,600
You don't know what you want.
None of you ever did.

246
00:22:08,360 --> 00:22:11,520
Mom, come quick!
Some weirdo broke into our house!

247
00:22:11,840 --> 00:22:13,480
Matty? What are you yelling about?

248
00:22:13,800 --> 00:22:15,840
There's a stranger
sitting at our table!

249
00:22:17,040 --> 00:22:18,080
That's your brother.

250
00:22:20,480 --> 00:22:22,280
Never seen him before in my life.

251
00:22:22,360 --> 00:22:24,800
It is rare that you're up and around
before noon, Terry

252
00:22:24,880 --> 00:22:26,440
what with your job and all.

253
00:22:26,520 --> 00:22:28,200
I'm not working
for Mr. Wayne anymore.

254
00:22:31,160 --> 00:22:33,520
Well, it will be nice
to have you home for a change.

255
00:22:33,600 --> 00:22:35,840
- Right, Matt?
- Sure. Great.

256
00:22:35,920 --> 00:22:38,240
Just when I was getting used
to being an only child.

257
00:22:40,560 --> 00:22:41,600
Mom!

258
00:22:47,960 --> 00:22:49,760
Every once in a while,
we have to do it, Dane.

259
00:22:49,840 --> 00:22:51,960
Ditch the guys
and have a night out to ourselves.

260
00:22:52,040 --> 00:22:53,800
It may be a change for you, Chelsea.

261
00:22:53,880 --> 00:22:56,040
I don't see enough of Terry
to know the difference.

262
00:22:56,120 --> 00:22:57,360
Well, Terry's sweet and all

263
00:22:57,440 --> 00:22:59,840
but who says you can't make friends
with someone new?

264
00:22:59,920 --> 00:23:00,960
Not a chance.

265
00:23:01,280 --> 00:23:02,280
Terry!

266
00:23:03,480 --> 00:23:05,240
I thought you'd be working as usual.

267
00:23:06,640 --> 00:23:07,960
The bad news is, for the time being

268
00:23:08,040 --> 00:23:09,520
I'm not gonna have
much money coming in.

269
00:23:09,960 --> 00:23:12,560
The good news is,
you have me all to yourself.

270
00:23:13,080 --> 00:23:14,240
I can live with that.

271
00:23:28,120 --> 00:23:29,200
Cutting in.

272
00:23:33,720 --> 00:23:34,720
Hey!

273
00:23:40,960 --> 00:23:41,960
Dana?

274
00:23:56,360 --> 00:23:57,360
What is it, boy?

275
00:23:59,200 --> 00:24:00,200
Ace.

276
00:24:03,560 --> 00:24:04,600
Ace!

277
00:24:31,360 --> 00:24:32,800
Don't get up, Bruce.

278
00:24:32,880 --> 00:24:35,760
It's just an old friend
come by to say hello.

279
00:24:43,880 --> 00:24:44,960
Hello...

280
00:24:45,560 --> 00:24:46,920
Batman.

281
00:24:52,040 --> 00:24:53,040
Dana!

282
00:24:55,240 --> 00:24:56,360
Watch it!

283
00:24:56,440 --> 00:24:57,520
It was her.

284
00:25:16,280 --> 00:25:17,360
- Hey!
- Terry!

285
00:25:17,960 --> 00:25:18,960
Dana!

286
00:25:20,720 --> 00:25:21,720
Let me go!

287
00:25:22,240 --> 00:25:23,320
Sure, cutes.

288
00:25:29,920 --> 00:25:30,920
Slag him!

289
00:25:45,120 --> 00:25:46,960
- Dana?
- Stay out of sight!

290
00:26:03,200 --> 00:26:04,200
There!

291
00:26:17,200 --> 00:26:19,480
- What's he doing?
- You got me.

292
00:26:20,880 --> 00:26:21,960
Just finish him!

293
00:26:41,680 --> 00:26:43,200
You made a mess, dreg.

294
00:26:53,520 --> 00:26:54,520
Dana!

295
00:26:54,600 --> 00:26:57,680
She's got a bad bump and some cuts,
but she's gonna be okay.

296
00:26:58,240 --> 00:27:00,800
- Why were those guys after you?
- I don't know.

297
00:27:01,200 --> 00:27:03,880
Look I'm gonna go talk to the cops.
Stay with her, okay, Chels?

298
00:27:03,960 --> 00:27:05,880
- I'll come as soon as I can.
- Sure.

299
00:27:21,960 --> 00:27:23,120
Leave a message.

300
00:27:23,480 --> 00:27:26,120
Hey, the Joker's little playmates
were after me tonight.

301
00:27:26,200 --> 00:27:27,640
Me, not Batman.

302
00:27:27,920 --> 00:27:29,920
This whole thing stinks, Wayne,
and you know why.

303
00:27:30,120 --> 00:27:31,520
I need some straight answers from...

304
00:27:32,160 --> 00:27:34,520
Wait, it's night. Where has he gone?

305
00:27:55,120 --> 00:27:56,120
Wayne?

306
00:27:56,400 --> 00:27:57,400
Wayne!

307
00:28:02,320 --> 00:28:03,320
Ace.

308
00:28:17,440 --> 00:28:18,720
Please, God, no.

309
00:28:46,800 --> 00:28:48,120
Floor...

310
00:28:51,400 --> 00:28:52,880
under...

311
00:28:54,960 --> 00:28:56,480
table.

312
00:29:30,240 --> 00:29:31,240
How is he?

313
00:29:31,600 --> 00:29:34,560
The antitoxin's done all it can.
It's up to him now.

314
00:29:35,080 --> 00:29:37,520
Thanks for coming.
I didn't know who else to call.

315
00:29:37,720 --> 00:29:38,720
Who else is there?

316
00:29:39,160 --> 00:29:41,840
That reminds me.
I better check on our other patient.

317
00:29:44,960 --> 00:29:46,320
What have I done?

318
00:29:47,480 --> 00:29:49,680
I killed the little rabbit.

319
00:29:50,600 --> 00:29:53,360
I don't deserve to live!

320
00:29:59,920 --> 00:30:01,040
How you doing, killer?

321
00:30:01,640 --> 00:30:04,240
I don't deserve to live!

322
00:30:04,880 --> 00:30:06,440
Yeah, rough night for me, too.

323
00:30:07,600 --> 00:30:09,760
Sad news from the financial world
this morning.

324
00:30:09,840 --> 00:30:12,120
The return of Bruce Wayne
to his family's company

325
00:30:12,200 --> 00:30:14,200
has been delayed due to an accident.

326
00:30:14,280 --> 00:30:16,960
Wayne Enterprises' Jordan Pryce
had this to say.

327
00:30:17,280 --> 00:30:20,720
We received a call from
Mr. Wayne's houseboy this morning

328
00:30:20,800 --> 00:30:23,080
saying Mr. Wayne
had taken a bad fall.

329
00:30:23,640 --> 00:30:25,640
Everyone
at the Wayne Enterprises family

330
00:30:25,720 --> 00:30:27,400
sends their prayers and good wishes

331
00:30:27,480 --> 00:30:30,480
to our senior member
for his speedy recovery.

332
00:30:31,640 --> 00:30:32,640
I'll bet.

333
00:30:32,960 --> 00:30:35,200
Not every creep in Gotham
wears a purple suit.

334
00:30:35,280 --> 00:30:37,040
It'd make my job simpler
if they did.

335
00:30:37,360 --> 00:30:41,360
The Joker knew about Bruce,
about me, probably about you too.

336
00:30:41,760 --> 00:30:43,240
Someone knows, I'll give you that.

337
00:30:43,720 --> 00:30:46,240
But it's not the Joker.
Not the real one.

338
00:30:46,760 --> 00:30:47,880
Bruce said he was dead.

339
00:30:49,880 --> 00:30:50,880
And?

340
00:30:50,960 --> 00:30:53,400
That's it. I know there's more.

341
00:30:54,160 --> 00:30:55,360
Barbara, I'm part of this.

342
00:30:55,440 --> 00:30:57,200
I need the answers
Bruce can't give me.

343
00:30:57,960 --> 00:30:58,960
I deserve them.

344
00:31:05,240 --> 00:31:07,720
I thought talking about it
would get easier over time

345
00:31:08,040 --> 00:31:09,680
but some hurts never go away.

346
00:31:11,120 --> 00:31:13,000
Dick Grayson, Nightwing

347
00:31:13,080 --> 00:31:15,360
had left to establish himself
in another city.

348
00:31:16,560 --> 00:31:17,680
There were three of us then.

349
00:31:17,760 --> 00:31:20,240
Bruce, myself,
and Robin, Tim Drake.

350
00:31:29,960 --> 00:31:31,200
Robin was out alone that night

351
00:31:31,280 --> 00:31:32,880
when he came upon a woman
in trouble.

352
00:31:33,960 --> 00:31:35,720
Help! Help!

353
00:31:36,320 --> 00:31:37,960
Somebody, please, help!

354
00:31:40,800 --> 00:31:41,840
Hero time.

355
00:31:48,360 --> 00:31:52,000
- That evens things up a little.
- Not really, bird-boy!

356
00:31:59,760 --> 00:32:01,320
A bird in the hand.

357
00:32:04,240 --> 00:32:06,080
We soon realized Tim was missing.

358
00:32:08,160 --> 00:32:10,600
Night after night,
we scoured the city

359
00:32:10,680 --> 00:32:12,160
running down every lead

360
00:32:12,240 --> 00:32:14,000
pressing every underworld connection.

361
00:32:18,080 --> 00:32:20,240
But no one had seen
any sign of Robin.

362
00:32:21,400 --> 00:32:24,080
For three agonizing weeks,
there was nothing.

363
00:32:24,760 --> 00:32:27,480
Then one night,
we were sent an invitation.

364
00:32:57,360 --> 00:32:58,440
Arkham.

365
00:33:00,240 --> 00:33:03,080
The asylum had been moved
to a newer, high-security building.

366
00:33:03,600 --> 00:33:06,080
The old building
had been partially demolished

367
00:33:06,160 --> 00:33:08,120
and hung open like a rotting wound.

368
00:33:15,040 --> 00:33:19,240
Hush, little baby, don't say a word

369
00:33:19,320 --> 00:33:23,520
Mama's gonna buy you a mockingbird

370
00:33:24,120 --> 00:33:27,920
And if that mockingbird don't sing

371
00:33:28,480 --> 00:33:32,560
Mama's gonna buy you a diamond ring

372
00:33:32,640 --> 00:33:37,840
And if that diamond ring turns brass

373
00:33:37,920 --> 00:33:42,360
Mama's gonna buy you a looking glass

374
00:33:42,640 --> 00:33:47,200
And if that looking glass gets broke

375
00:33:49,320 --> 00:33:51,360
Pudding, company!

376
00:33:53,880 --> 00:33:57,360
Hello there!
Welcome to our happy home.

377
00:34:01,640 --> 00:34:02,880
Where's Robin?

378
00:34:03,680 --> 00:34:04,720
Robin?

379
00:34:05,240 --> 00:34:06,760
There's no Robin here.

380
00:34:06,840 --> 00:34:08,840
Maybe he means our little J.

381
00:34:09,160 --> 00:34:10,920
Of course! That's it!

382
00:34:16,640 --> 00:34:17,800
No peeking.

383
00:34:26,880 --> 00:34:28,640
Mommy's little helper.

384
00:34:31,440 --> 00:34:35,440
You know, Bats, we've been doing this
little runaround of ours for years.

385
00:34:35,520 --> 00:34:38,680
It's been loads of laughs,
but the sad fact is

386
00:34:38,760 --> 00:34:40,440
none of us are getting any younger.

387
00:34:40,760 --> 00:34:42,760
That old clock's a-ticking.

388
00:34:42,840 --> 00:34:44,360
Quite right, pooh.

389
00:34:44,640 --> 00:34:48,040
And Harley and I were thinking
it was time to start a family.

390
00:34:48,120 --> 00:34:51,160
Add a Joker Junior
to our merry brood.

391
00:34:51,560 --> 00:34:54,640
But rather than go through
all the joy of childbirth

392
00:34:54,720 --> 00:34:56,320
we decided to adopt.

393
00:34:58,720 --> 00:35:00,360
We couldn't do it legally

394
00:35:00,440 --> 00:35:04,720
but then we remembered you always
had a few spare kids hanging around.

395
00:35:04,920 --> 00:35:06,480
So we borrowed one.

396
00:35:10,960 --> 00:35:12,000
No.

397
00:35:12,080 --> 00:35:13,600
My God!

398
00:35:13,840 --> 00:35:18,280
He needed a little molding,
of course. What kid doesn't?

399
00:35:18,360 --> 00:35:21,280
But in time,
we came to love him as our own.

400
00:35:21,680 --> 00:35:23,920
Say hello, J.J.

401
00:35:52,640 --> 00:35:54,080
Robin! Robin!

402
00:35:57,120 --> 00:36:00,240
Tim, it's Barbara. Can you hear me?

403
00:36:13,440 --> 00:36:15,080
Robin! Stop!

404
00:36:16,200 --> 00:36:17,960
Hands off, Brat-girl!

405
00:36:18,360 --> 00:36:20,760
Sweetie, get Mommy's bazooka.

406
00:36:44,280 --> 00:36:46,160
How could you help
Joker do it, Harley?

407
00:36:46,680 --> 00:36:50,120
Okay, so he roughed the kid up
a little, but I'll make it right.

408
00:36:50,560 --> 00:36:52,960
Yeah, you're Mother
of the stinking Year.

409
00:36:53,720 --> 00:36:54,800
You'll see.

410
00:36:56,520 --> 00:36:59,200
We'll be one big, happy family.

411
00:37:05,480 --> 00:37:06,600
Good boy!

412
00:37:55,160 --> 00:37:56,880
What's the matter, Batman?

413
00:37:57,920 --> 00:38:00,800
No witty comeback? No threat?

414
00:38:04,520 --> 00:38:06,280
Then I'll provide the narration.

415
00:38:10,880 --> 00:38:14,600
I'll begin with how I affected
young Robin's makeover.

416
00:38:16,600 --> 00:38:19,240
Though he bravely tried
to fight it, at first.

417
00:38:19,320 --> 00:38:22,600
You would have been proud
to see him so strong!

418
00:38:25,320 --> 00:38:27,040
But all too soon

419
00:38:27,120 --> 00:38:31,360
the dear lad began to share
such secrets with me.

420
00:38:31,440 --> 00:38:34,640
Secrets that are mine alone
to know...

421
00:38:34,960 --> 00:38:36,080
Bruce.

422
00:38:36,720 --> 00:38:39,960
It's true, Batsy. I know everything.

423
00:38:40,120 --> 00:38:43,160
And kinda like the kid
who peeks at his Christmas presents

424
00:38:43,240 --> 00:38:46,680
I must admit,
it's sadly anticlimactic.

425
00:38:46,760 --> 00:38:49,560
Behind all the Sturm and batarangs

426
00:38:49,640 --> 00:38:51,800
you're just a little boy
in a playsuit

427
00:38:51,880 --> 00:38:53,960
crying for Mommy and Daddy.

428
00:38:54,480 --> 00:38:56,800
It'd be funny
if it weren't so pathetic.

429
00:38:58,480 --> 00:39:00,920
Oh, what the heck, I'll laugh anyway.

430
00:39:14,960 --> 00:39:18,240
If you don't like the movie,
I've got slides.

431
00:39:29,480 --> 00:39:31,600
I'll break you in two.

432
00:39:31,960 --> 00:39:33,560
Oh, Batman.

433
00:39:33,640 --> 00:39:35,480
If you have the guts
for that kind of fun

434
00:39:35,560 --> 00:39:37,400
you'd have done it years ago.

435
00:39:37,480 --> 00:39:39,200
I, on the other hand...

436
00:39:47,160 --> 00:39:48,920
You've lost, Batman.

437
00:39:49,240 --> 00:39:50,720
Robin is mine.

438
00:39:51,080 --> 00:39:54,720
The last sound you hear
will be our laughter.

439
00:39:57,160 --> 00:39:58,840
Here you go, sonny-boy.

440
00:40:01,640 --> 00:40:03,320
Make him one of us.

441
00:40:45,040 --> 00:40:46,040
It's okay, Tim.

442
00:40:46,800 --> 00:40:47,840
It's okay.

443
00:40:50,320 --> 00:40:52,760
The only other person who knew
what happened was my father

444
00:40:52,840 --> 00:40:54,400
the first Commissioner Gordon.

445
00:40:54,480 --> 00:40:56,920
And for Robin's sake,
he kept that night a secret.

446
00:40:58,960 --> 00:41:00,960
With his last act of cruelty

447
00:41:01,040 --> 00:41:04,920
the Joker had tainted us all
with compromise and deception.

448
00:41:08,680 --> 00:41:10,880
I suppose he had
the last laugh after all.

449
00:41:11,160 --> 00:41:13,280
And since you saw Harley
fall into the pit...

450
00:41:13,360 --> 00:41:16,560
We never found her body, but I doubt
she'd be starting trouble now.

451
00:41:19,280 --> 00:41:21,200
- And Tim?
- We had a trusted friend

452
00:41:21,280 --> 00:41:22,680
Dr. Leslie Thompkins.

453
00:41:22,760 --> 00:41:26,200
It took her a year, but she was able
to help Tim back to himself.

454
00:41:26,600 --> 00:41:28,880
Still, things were never
really the same.

455
00:41:29,280 --> 00:41:31,520
Bruce forbade Tim to be Robin again.

456
00:41:31,880 --> 00:41:33,400
He blamed himself for what happened

457
00:41:33,480 --> 00:41:35,960
and swore he'd never endanger
another young partner.

458
00:41:36,520 --> 00:41:39,760
Tim left us soon after that,
determined to make it on his own.

459
00:41:40,360 --> 00:41:41,880
Did they ever patch things up?

460
00:41:41,960 --> 00:41:44,240
Tim tried once or twice,
but you know Bruce.

461
00:41:44,840 --> 00:41:46,480
I check up on Tim now and then.

462
00:41:46,560 --> 00:41:49,720
He's a top-level communications
engineer, married, couple kids.

463
00:41:50,320 --> 00:41:52,160
Not too bad, all things concerned.

464
00:41:52,520 --> 00:41:53,840
He deserved a happy ending.

465
00:41:54,560 --> 00:41:56,920
But he still has the most likely
connection to that night.

466
00:42:06,640 --> 00:42:09,200
It looks okay on this side.
I'm going up to the dish.

467
00:42:20,920 --> 00:42:23,680
You might as well show yourself.
I heard you a mile away.

468
00:42:25,200 --> 00:42:26,600
I'm no Boy Wonder anymore

469
00:42:26,680 --> 00:42:28,720
but that old training
never goes away.

470
00:42:28,800 --> 00:42:29,840
Even at my age.

471
00:42:30,840 --> 00:42:31,840
Tim Drake.

472
00:42:32,240 --> 00:42:33,520
You heard about Bruce?

473
00:42:34,080 --> 00:42:36,360
Barbara told me. That was too bad.

474
00:42:36,840 --> 00:42:37,920
You're not too broken up.

475
00:42:38,400 --> 00:42:40,880
I had nothing to do with it,
despite what you might be thinking.

476
00:42:41,400 --> 00:42:44,200
When the Joker reappeared,
I was just as surprised as anyone.

477
00:42:44,760 --> 00:42:46,640
Barb told you the gory details?

478
00:42:47,120 --> 00:42:48,200
More or less.

479
00:42:48,720 --> 00:42:51,600
Look, it's been almost 40 years.
It wasn't easy

480
00:42:51,680 --> 00:42:54,320
but I managed to put it to bed
and go on with my life.

481
00:42:54,640 --> 00:42:56,320
You'll have to do it yourself,
one day.

482
00:42:56,920 --> 00:42:59,520
We all did. We gave our best

483
00:42:59,600 --> 00:43:02,000
but in the end, that wasn't
good enough for the old man.

484
00:43:02,920 --> 00:43:04,280
Regrets, Mr. Drake?

485
00:43:05,240 --> 00:43:06,600
When I was younger,
part of me thought

486
00:43:06,680 --> 00:43:08,480
I would go on and on, and someday...

487
00:43:09,800 --> 00:43:12,800
Capes, costumes, playing hero.
It was kid stuff.

488
00:43:13,400 --> 00:43:14,960
Bruce probably did me a favor.

489
00:43:15,320 --> 00:43:16,640
In the end, I was so sick of it

490
00:43:16,720 --> 00:43:19,040
I never wanted to see
that stupid Robin suit again.

491
00:43:22,000 --> 00:43:23,680
Some things never change.

492
00:43:25,720 --> 00:43:27,520
Were all of you that bitter
when you left?

493
00:43:28,080 --> 00:43:30,000
Comes with the territory, McGinnis.

494
00:43:30,080 --> 00:43:32,320
Look up Nightwing, someday.
Has he got stories.

495
00:43:32,400 --> 00:43:35,240
Drake's clean anyway.
I've got one more lead to check out.

496
00:43:35,320 --> 00:43:37,840
Someone with a definite grudge
to hold against Bruce Wayne.

497
00:43:48,080 --> 00:43:49,080
You?

498
00:43:50,360 --> 00:43:51,360
Where's Amy?

499
00:43:52,400 --> 00:43:53,880
Missed the boat, I'm afraid.

500
00:43:57,840 --> 00:43:59,160
Turn the yacht around!

501
00:43:59,240 --> 00:44:00,720
Detox, boss man.

502
00:44:01,480 --> 00:44:03,000
We're here to talk business.

503
00:44:03,080 --> 00:44:05,680
We'll be quick.
Woof gets seasick easy.

504
00:44:08,680 --> 00:44:10,520
Our business is concluded.

505
00:44:18,120 --> 00:44:19,800
You got the equipment you wanted.

506
00:44:19,880 --> 00:44:23,320
I gave you the security codes
so you could ransack the lab

507
00:44:23,400 --> 00:44:25,720
while those bunglers tried
to ice Wayne.

508
00:44:26,440 --> 00:44:28,600
Word is, Wayne's terminal anyhow.

509
00:44:30,360 --> 00:44:32,360
That means you get to stay top dog.

510
00:44:32,880 --> 00:44:34,240
And everyone's happy.

511
00:44:34,760 --> 00:44:36,040
So why are you here?

512
00:44:36,400 --> 00:44:38,600
The big guy
who originally put us all in contact

513
00:44:38,680 --> 00:44:40,240
just decided you're a loose end.

514
00:44:41,160 --> 00:44:43,280
And loose ends should be tied up.

515
00:44:50,440 --> 00:44:51,600
Let me go!

516
00:44:52,080 --> 00:44:53,120
Got him.

517
00:44:53,560 --> 00:44:55,880
Then am-scray pronto, kiddies.

518
00:44:59,640 --> 00:45:01,640
Things are going to start popping.

519
00:45:02,040 --> 00:45:03,120
Let's go!

520
00:45:05,160 --> 00:45:07,280
No one's leaving until I get answers.

521
00:45:11,520 --> 00:45:13,360
No, you idiot! Not now!

522
00:45:22,440 --> 00:45:23,720
They're getting away!

523
00:45:24,840 --> 00:45:26,640
Yeah, and I think
they've got a good reason!

524
00:45:29,680 --> 00:45:30,840
What's happening?

525
00:45:30,920 --> 00:45:31,960
Hang on!

526
00:46:13,440 --> 00:46:15,040
We saw the explosion.

527
00:46:15,120 --> 00:46:16,800
You can ask Mr. Pryce about that.

528
00:46:17,320 --> 00:46:19,560
Me? I had nothing to do with it.

529
00:46:19,640 --> 00:46:20,640
That right?

530
00:46:21,600 --> 00:46:25,080
I gave you the security codes
so you could ransack the lab

531
00:46:25,160 --> 00:46:27,560
while those bunglers tried
to ice Wayne.

532
00:46:27,680 --> 00:46:28,840
I want my lawyer.

533
00:46:28,920 --> 00:46:32,400
I think the commissioner
would like to hear this too. Night.

534
00:46:48,720 --> 00:46:49,800
I'm spent.

535
00:46:50,600 --> 00:46:53,360
Every lead I had has gone face down,
and the Joker's still out there.

536
00:46:54,120 --> 00:46:55,120
What have you got?

537
00:46:56,240 --> 00:46:57,240
I don't know, pup.

538
00:46:57,880 --> 00:46:59,160
If I was the Batman
I was supposed to be

539
00:46:59,240 --> 00:47:00,560
I'd have cracked this by now.

540
00:47:01,080 --> 00:47:03,680
Would have punched exactly
the right data into the computer

541
00:47:03,760 --> 00:47:06,280
or remembered that one little clue
that everyone else overlooked.

542
00:47:07,120 --> 00:47:08,840
It's rarely that simple.

543
00:47:15,400 --> 00:47:17,320
- How are you feeling?
- Lousy.

544
00:47:20,040 --> 00:47:21,600
Gordon told me what happened
to Tim Drake.

545
00:47:22,360 --> 00:47:25,200
That's why I didn't want you
going up against the Joker.

546
00:47:25,880 --> 00:47:27,400
Impostor or not.

547
00:47:27,480 --> 00:47:29,080
Nothing against your old partners

548
00:47:29,160 --> 00:47:30,680
but I'm a completely
different Batman.

549
00:47:31,160 --> 00:47:32,720
I was never a Robin, I never...

550
00:47:36,200 --> 00:47:37,240
Wait.

551
00:47:38,360 --> 00:47:40,240
Joker smashed up the cases

552
00:47:40,320 --> 00:47:43,160
but why was this the only costume
he went out of his way to destroy?

553
00:47:43,240 --> 00:47:44,840
Robin defeated him.

554
00:47:44,920 --> 00:47:48,440
A ghost out for revenge?
I don't buy it. I talked to Drake.

555
00:47:48,520 --> 00:47:50,560
He's got less love
for that costume than the Joker.

556
00:47:51,280 --> 00:47:52,920
I think somehow he's behind this.

557
00:47:53,600 --> 00:47:54,760
That's crazy.

558
00:47:54,840 --> 00:47:57,000
So was Drake, once.

559
00:47:57,080 --> 00:47:59,120
Look, here's the readout
of everything we know

560
00:47:59,200 --> 00:48:00,400
the Jokerz have stolen.

561
00:48:03,360 --> 00:48:05,120
Now let's combine those
into something that would be used

562
00:48:05,200 --> 00:48:06,600
by a communications expert.

563
00:48:07,000 --> 00:48:08,720
Someone of Tim Drake's caliber.

564
00:48:11,360 --> 00:48:13,120
Satellite jamming system.

565
00:48:13,360 --> 00:48:16,200
Whoever uses this
can access satellite defense systems

566
00:48:16,280 --> 00:48:17,480
and fire them at will.

567
00:48:17,920 --> 00:48:19,360
Someone already has.

568
00:48:19,440 --> 00:48:21,520
I suspected Jordan Pryce
might be the Joker

569
00:48:21,600 --> 00:48:24,560
but the Jokerz were on your
company yacht trying to slag Pryce.

570
00:48:24,640 --> 00:48:27,040
I got him off the boat before
someone blasted it into splinters.

571
00:48:30,240 --> 00:48:32,000
I hate to say it
but I think your little Robin's

572
00:48:32,080 --> 00:48:33,320
turned into a bitter old crow.

573
00:48:33,960 --> 00:48:36,080
He's gotta be the brains
behind this new Joker.

574
00:48:36,160 --> 00:48:38,520
It's harsh, but who else is there?

575
00:48:41,040 --> 00:48:42,040
Suit up.

576
00:48:42,680 --> 00:48:45,600
Take the car and check it out.
I'll monitor you from here.

577
00:48:47,280 --> 00:48:48,600
What happened
to leaving it to the cops?

578
00:48:49,800 --> 00:48:50,920
Not their game.

579
00:48:51,480 --> 00:48:53,160
There's something else
I want to take with me.

580
00:49:17,200 --> 00:49:19,960
Drake, I know you're the connection
to the Joker.

581
00:49:22,360 --> 00:49:24,040
Don't pretend you didn't hear me.

582
00:49:25,080 --> 00:49:26,080
Hologram.

583
00:49:40,000 --> 00:49:41,840
You guessed it, Batfake!

584
00:49:42,200 --> 00:49:45,560
The disgruntled Mr. Drake
is indeed in my employ.

585
00:49:46,040 --> 00:49:47,240
Took him a few years

586
00:49:47,320 --> 00:49:51,040
but he finally figured out
who ran the real winning team.

587
00:49:51,120 --> 00:49:54,640
This is one of Uncle Sam's
orbiting defense satellites.

588
00:49:54,720 --> 00:49:57,200
Hyperion class, laser-armed.

589
00:49:57,280 --> 00:49:59,800
Handy little gadget
for shooting down unfriendly missiles

590
00:49:59,880 --> 00:50:02,440
or giving someone
a world-class hotfoot.

591
00:50:04,800 --> 00:50:08,120
Think of it as urban tagging
on a grand scale

592
00:50:08,200 --> 00:50:12,920
reminding all and sundry
that this is Joker territory.

593
00:50:13,000 --> 00:50:14,400
You're welcome to try and stop us

594
00:50:14,480 --> 00:50:17,960
but I'm not taking bets
on that happening anytime soon.

595
00:50:18,040 --> 00:50:19,280
Toodles.

596
00:51:10,680 --> 00:51:11,680
Miss me?

597
00:51:20,760 --> 00:51:22,960
Computer,
search for the name Jolly Jack.

598
00:51:28,240 --> 00:51:31,600
Abandoned candy factory.
Just his style.

599
00:51:31,680 --> 00:51:33,360
Wayne, I think I've got something.

600
00:51:33,440 --> 00:51:34,440
Download this transmission

601
00:51:34,520 --> 00:51:36,320
and tell Gordon to have her men
at that address.

602
00:51:36,640 --> 00:51:39,560
- I'm gonna...
- Aren't you the nasty tattletale?

603
00:51:39,640 --> 00:51:42,600
Ratting me out before I have my fun.

604
00:51:43,040 --> 00:51:44,600
Papa spank.

605
00:52:02,880 --> 00:52:03,960
Yeah, I know!

606
00:52:45,160 --> 00:52:47,400
I better sit down
before I bust a gut.

607
00:52:48,440 --> 00:52:49,920
Catch you later, kiddo.

608
00:52:54,360 --> 00:52:56,400
It stopped. I'm going after him.

609
00:53:18,120 --> 00:53:19,120
Gotcha.

610
00:53:41,560 --> 00:53:42,680
Ace.

611
00:53:52,880 --> 00:53:54,120
Good bad-dog.

612
00:54:04,280 --> 00:54:05,360
Where'd he go?

613
00:54:10,080 --> 00:54:11,080
Watch it!

614
00:54:11,320 --> 00:54:12,400
You watch it!

615
00:54:14,840 --> 00:54:15,840
It's him!

616
00:54:34,400 --> 00:54:35,600
Double down.

617
00:54:53,000 --> 00:54:55,200
Lovely playroom.
You getting this, Wayne?

618
00:54:55,800 --> 00:54:56,840
I see it.

619
00:54:56,920 --> 00:54:58,440
You keep your eyes open
for the Joker.

620
00:55:08,880 --> 00:55:09,880
Tim.

621
00:55:10,400 --> 00:55:11,400
Get up, Drake.

622
00:55:12,960 --> 00:55:14,720
What? Who is it?

623
00:55:15,240 --> 00:55:16,600
Where's the Joker?

624
00:55:17,040 --> 00:55:18,040
Joker?

625
00:55:18,120 --> 00:55:20,600
Drop the act.
I know you're working with him.

626
00:55:21,120 --> 00:55:22,680
No, Joker's gone.

627
00:55:23,080 --> 00:55:24,520
I don't know where he is, really.

628
00:55:25,080 --> 00:55:27,800
The suit sensors aren't picking up
any pulse fluctuations.

629
00:55:28,280 --> 00:55:29,480
He's telling the truth.

630
00:55:29,800 --> 00:55:33,040
I don't do this anymore.
I have a home and family.

631
00:55:33,120 --> 00:55:36,480
I gave this up years ago.
Kid stuff. That's all it was.

632
00:55:37,520 --> 00:55:39,880
He may be telling the truth,
but he's still whacked.

633
00:55:40,280 --> 00:55:41,360
Fun and games.

634
00:55:41,880 --> 00:55:43,760
Boy Wonder playing the hero.

635
00:55:43,840 --> 00:55:46,240
Fighting the bad guys
and no one ever gets...

636
00:55:47,280 --> 00:55:48,440
Oh, God.

637
00:55:49,360 --> 00:55:50,560
I did it.

638
00:55:51,360 --> 00:55:52,680
I didn't mean to.

639
00:55:53,200 --> 00:55:55,040
I tried so hard to forget.

640
00:55:55,240 --> 00:55:59,000
But I can still hear the scream,
still see his frozen smile.

641
00:55:59,800 --> 00:56:01,680
Every night, the dreams get stronger.

642
00:56:01,760 --> 00:56:04,360
He's there when I sleep,
whispering, laughing

643
00:56:04,440 --> 00:56:07,200
telling me I'm just as bad as he is,
we're both the same.

644
00:56:07,520 --> 00:56:08,920
I'm calling an ambulance.

645
00:56:09,440 --> 00:56:11,920
No, I'm all right. Forgive me, Terry.

646
00:56:12,000 --> 00:56:15,320
Old, nasty memories twisting
inside me like bad oysters.

647
00:56:15,840 --> 00:56:16,920
Nothing, really.

648
00:56:17,400 --> 00:56:18,720
I'm perfectly fine now.

649
00:56:19,280 --> 00:56:20,680
How do you know my name?

650
00:56:21,120 --> 00:56:23,920
There's nothing about you
I don't know, Batfake.

651
00:56:28,880 --> 00:56:29,880
Terry!

652
00:56:31,840 --> 00:56:33,400
Have a time-out, kid.

653
00:56:33,680 --> 00:56:35,800
Can't let you spoil
the party too soon.

654
00:56:36,520 --> 00:56:40,760
And Bruce, I'm sure you've got
your monkey-boy wired somehow.

655
00:56:41,360 --> 00:56:42,800
That's just peachy

656
00:56:42,880 --> 00:56:45,440
'cause I want you to see
every minute of this.

657
00:56:45,680 --> 00:56:46,800
It's a doozy.

658
00:57:04,480 --> 00:57:05,760
My God.

659
00:57:09,520 --> 00:57:12,520
Oh, I never get tired of that!

660
00:57:12,960 --> 00:57:14,040
Drake?

661
00:57:14,440 --> 00:57:15,600
You're the Joker?

662
00:57:16,560 --> 00:57:20,760
That flabby oaf doesn't even realize
I'm using him as a timeshare.

663
00:57:20,840 --> 00:57:25,040
Beneath this puckish exterior
lies the mind of a genius

664
00:57:25,120 --> 00:57:26,640
years ahead of my time.

665
00:57:26,960 --> 00:57:29,840
In the weeks young Robin
was under my tutelage

666
00:57:29,920 --> 00:57:33,920
I used him as the subject
of my greatest experiment.

667
00:57:34,480 --> 00:57:37,400
Utilizing cutting-edge
genetics technology

668
00:57:37,480 --> 00:57:39,400
which I had pinched here and there

669
00:57:39,480 --> 00:57:42,520
I encoded my DNA on a microchip

670
00:57:42,600 --> 00:57:45,680
and set it into bird-boy's birdbrain.

671
00:57:46,280 --> 00:57:47,640
Here.

672
00:57:47,720 --> 00:57:52,400
Everything that was me has been
a-sleeping all comfy and cozy

673
00:57:52,480 --> 00:57:55,240
inside Tim Drake's subconscious.

674
00:57:55,400 --> 00:57:59,040
At first, I had to limit the time
I spent in Drake's body.

675
00:57:59,560 --> 00:58:01,200
He's not aware of what I do

676
00:58:01,280 --> 00:58:04,280
chalking up any lingering memories
to bad dreams.

677
00:58:04,360 --> 00:58:07,560
If his family misses him,
I simply call wifey and tell her

678
00:58:07,640 --> 00:58:08,880
"I'm working late, honey."

679
00:58:10,000 --> 00:58:12,080
The changes come at will now

680
00:58:12,160 --> 00:58:16,080
and soon I'll be strong enough
to live in this body permanently.

681
00:58:16,320 --> 00:58:18,960
Mr. J's on the rebound, baby!

682
00:58:19,280 --> 00:58:22,920
My comeback party's gonna set
the whole town on fire!

683
00:58:44,760 --> 00:58:47,200
So where should I make ground zero?

684
00:58:47,280 --> 00:58:51,400
Gotham General, where our hero's
dear little Dana is recuperating?

685
00:58:51,480 --> 00:58:55,320
Or here, in the happy garden
of Mrs. Mary McGinnis?

686
00:58:57,600 --> 00:59:01,000
I always think it adds resonance
to a hero's mission

687
00:59:01,080 --> 00:59:04,040
to have some defining element
of tragedy in his background.

688
00:59:04,320 --> 00:59:05,320
Don't you?

689
00:59:07,640 --> 00:59:10,000
But the one and only kick-off point

690
00:59:10,080 --> 00:59:12,800
must be stately Wayne Manor.

691
00:59:12,880 --> 00:59:14,240
Gone in a flash

692
00:59:14,320 --> 00:59:18,120
before Brucie can hobble to safety
or mount a rescue.

693
00:59:18,720 --> 00:59:19,880
Don't worry, though.

694
00:59:22,760 --> 00:59:25,440
I'll be hitting
those other spots soon enough.

695
00:59:26,800 --> 00:59:28,120
Adiós, Brucie.

696
00:59:28,560 --> 00:59:31,920
I guess I should salute you
as a worthy adversary and all that

697
00:59:32,000 --> 00:59:35,520
but the truth is,
I really did hate your guts.

698
00:59:37,920 --> 00:59:42,080
What about it, kid?
Any last words for the old Bat-coot?

699
00:59:42,560 --> 00:59:44,080
Yeah. Sic him.

700
00:59:50,520 --> 00:59:51,800
Ace, here!

701
00:59:55,480 --> 00:59:56,600
Attaboy!

702
01:00:09,200 --> 01:00:11,240
End of the line, Snoopy.

703
01:00:17,600 --> 01:00:18,600
No!

704
01:00:33,120 --> 01:00:34,720
Oh, good.

705
01:00:34,800 --> 01:00:36,360
The beam's headed here.

706
01:00:36,440 --> 01:00:39,200
Now I'll have
to start all over again.

707
01:00:39,280 --> 01:00:42,480
Thanks for wrecking everything, kid.
See you around.

708
01:00:42,760 --> 01:00:43,880
Hold it.

709
01:00:44,560 --> 01:00:47,840
Oh, wise up, Junior. Game's over!

710
01:00:47,920 --> 01:00:50,520
- I'm taking you in.
- Right.

711
01:00:57,000 --> 01:00:59,160
You're out of your league, McGinnis.

712
01:00:59,240 --> 01:01:03,400
I know every trick the original
Batman and Robin knew at their peak.

713
01:01:04,320 --> 01:01:06,800
Maybe, but you don't know
a thing about me.

714
01:01:07,080 --> 01:01:09,240
You? What's to know?

715
01:01:09,320 --> 01:01:11,920
You're a punk. A rank amateur.

716
01:01:12,000 --> 01:01:16,200
A costumed errand boy taking orders
from a senile old man.

717
01:01:16,280 --> 01:01:18,800
Still, if it's a whooping
you're a-wanting...

718
01:01:20,440 --> 01:01:23,680
That's right.
Better to run and save yourself.

719
01:01:23,800 --> 01:01:25,440
That's about your speed.

720
01:01:27,800 --> 01:01:29,280
Let's dance, bozo.

721
01:01:44,520 --> 01:01:46,760
He's tough. Any suggestions, boss?

722
01:01:46,840 --> 01:01:48,320
Joker is vain and likes to talk.

723
01:01:48,400 --> 01:01:50,080
He'll try to distract you,
but don't listen.

724
01:01:50,240 --> 01:01:51,920
Block it out and power on through.

725
01:01:52,200 --> 01:01:54,640
Wait. I like to talk, too.

726
01:01:57,800 --> 01:02:00,160
- What are you doing?
- Fighting dirty.

727
01:02:00,240 --> 01:02:02,040
The real Batman would never...

728
01:02:02,960 --> 01:02:04,440
Told you, you didn't know me.

729
01:02:07,120 --> 01:02:08,800
Funny guy.

730
01:02:09,400 --> 01:02:10,840
Can't say the same for you.

731
01:02:12,680 --> 01:02:15,880
Impudent brat.
Who do you think you're talking to?

732
01:02:16,440 --> 01:02:18,080
Not a comedian, I'll tell ya that.

733
01:02:19,520 --> 01:02:20,640
Shut your mouth!

734
01:02:22,080 --> 01:02:24,920
The real Batman
never talked to you much, did he?

735
01:02:25,000 --> 01:02:27,120
That's probably why
you were so fixated on him.

736
01:02:28,520 --> 01:02:31,440
Don't play psychoanalyst
with me, boy!

737
01:02:31,720 --> 01:02:33,960
Oh, I don't need a degree
to figure you out.

738
01:02:37,120 --> 01:02:38,720
The real reason you kept coming back

739
01:02:38,800 --> 01:02:40,760
was you never got a laugh
out of the old man.

740
01:02:41,680 --> 01:02:43,560
I'm not hearing this.

741
01:02:43,640 --> 01:02:46,520
Get a clue, clownie.
He's got no sense of humor.

742
01:02:46,600 --> 01:02:48,520
He wouldn't know a good joke
if it bit him in the cape.

743
01:02:49,480 --> 01:02:50,960
Not that you ever had a good joke.

744
01:02:51,040 --> 01:02:52,800
Shut up. Shut up!

745
01:02:52,880 --> 01:02:55,680
I mean, joy buzzers,
squirting flowers? Lame!

746
01:02:55,760 --> 01:02:57,080
Where's the A-material?

747
01:02:57,160 --> 01:02:59,640
Make a face,
drop your pants, something!

748
01:02:59,720 --> 01:03:00,760
Show yourself!

749
01:03:00,840 --> 01:03:04,360
You make me laugh, but only 'cause
I think you're kind of pathetic.

750
01:03:07,200 --> 01:03:08,480
Stop that!

751
01:03:10,040 --> 01:03:12,720
So, you fell in a tank of acid,
got your skin bleached

752
01:03:12,800 --> 01:03:14,760
then decided to become
a supervillain.

753
01:03:14,840 --> 01:03:17,080
What? You couldn't get work
as a rodeo clown?

754
01:03:20,880 --> 01:03:22,600
Don't you dare laugh at me!

755
01:03:24,920 --> 01:03:28,360
Why? I thought the Joker
always wanted to make Batman laugh.

756
01:03:28,440 --> 01:03:30,160
You're not Batman!

757
01:03:54,080 --> 01:03:55,600
Come on, McGinnis!

758
01:03:55,680 --> 01:03:59,080
Laugh it up now,
you miserable little punk! Laugh!

759
01:04:00,200 --> 01:04:03,520
I can't hear you!

760
01:04:33,280 --> 01:04:34,560
Easy, I've got ya.

761
01:04:44,160 --> 01:04:45,400
Way ahead of you, mutt.

762
01:05:36,280 --> 01:05:39,200
Delia and Deidre Dennis,
your grandmother's paid your bail

763
01:05:39,280 --> 01:05:41,920
and you're being released
into her custody, pending your trial.

764
01:05:42,080 --> 01:05:43,600
- Oh...
- Joy.

765
01:05:47,160 --> 01:05:49,160
You rotten little scamps!

766
01:05:49,240 --> 01:05:51,080
I struggle to make
a good home for you

767
01:05:51,160 --> 01:05:52,880
and this is the thanks I get!

768
01:05:54,600 --> 01:05:56,080
Break a grandmother's heart!

769
01:05:56,160 --> 01:05:57,880
I hope they throw the book at you!

770
01:05:58,120 --> 01:06:00,040
Oh, shut up, Nana Harley.

771
01:06:04,600 --> 01:06:06,640
You didn't have
to cover up for me, Barbara.

772
01:06:06,840 --> 01:06:10,000
The Joker's gone, Tim.
You were just along for the ride.

773
01:06:12,040 --> 01:06:13,200
How are you doing, Mr. Drake?

774
01:06:13,480 --> 01:06:15,320
Tim, this is Terry McGinnis.

775
01:06:15,520 --> 01:06:17,600
- We met the other night.
- We did?

776
01:06:20,680 --> 01:06:22,120
I owe you big time.

777
01:06:22,680 --> 01:06:23,760
Forget it.

778
01:06:23,960 --> 01:06:25,200
For what it's worth

779
01:06:25,280 --> 01:06:27,880
Bruce couldn't have chosen
anyone better to put on the mask.

780
01:06:28,880 --> 01:06:31,360
Coming from you,
that means everything.

781
01:06:32,280 --> 01:06:34,600
Sometimes
the important things go unsaid.

782
01:06:35,600 --> 01:06:37,160
If there's one thing I've learned

783
01:06:37,240 --> 01:06:38,960
you've got to appreciate
the people in your life

784
01:06:39,040 --> 01:06:40,400
while you have the chance.

785
01:06:40,880 --> 01:06:43,640
Not everyone is capable
of expressing that, Tim.

786
01:06:43,720 --> 01:06:45,840
No matter how much
they might feel it in their heart.

787
01:06:46,720 --> 01:06:47,760
I know.

788
01:06:52,040 --> 01:06:53,200
What are you doing here?

789
01:06:53,480 --> 01:06:54,800
It's where I should be.

790
01:06:58,280 --> 01:06:59,360
Terry.

791
01:07:00,800 --> 01:07:03,280
I've been thinking about
something you once told me.

792
01:07:04,360 --> 01:07:05,560
And you were wrong.

793
01:07:06,440 --> 01:07:08,520
It's not Batman
that makes you worthwhile.

794
01:07:09,640 --> 01:07:11,000
It's the other way around.

795
01:07:11,840 --> 01:07:14,040
Never tell yourself
anything different.

796
01:07:15,200 --> 01:07:16,280
Thanks.

797
01:07:24,040 --> 01:07:25,160
Hello, Tim.

798
01:07:26,520 --> 01:07:27,720
Hi, old man.

799
01:07:37,744 --> 01:07:45,744
Translator: IYUNO
